  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Postia Secoguaianolide and Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, as the compound is implicated in targeting multiple antigens, including CD70, which in turn is targeted by Scalarolide and Epicoccin C. These secondary targets are all known to interact with Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, indicating a possible pathway through which Postia Secoguaianolide may exert its effects. The scores from the three paths are consistent, suggesting a robust association, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role for Postia Secoguaianolide in modulating the activity of Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, though further experimental validation is required to confirm this relationship.",
